+/*
+ * plat_rk3036g.c -- RK3036G (ARM Cortex-A7, HDMI-only) platform layer.
+ *
+ * Direction-A port (charter §0.4): clean self-contained platform backend
+ * for the RK3036G CubeGM handheld, replacing the SF2000 transitional
+ * patches (cubevol shm input / /dev/dis display / driver.so audio).
+ *
+ * Structure mirrors the upstream plat_sf3000.c (which `#include "plat_sdl.c"`
+ * at the end): define the SDL keyboard binds + the evdev gamepad binds, then
+ * pull in the shared SDL implementation. SDL drives the keyboard/panel; evdev
+ * auto-supports any standard HID USB gamepad via BTN_* / ABS_* codes.
+ *
+ * Hardware facts (payload-305/307 device diag_report.txt + cubevol_bridge.c
+ * stock profile 0810_0001_0110):
+ *   - SoC: RK3036 dual Cortex-A7 @ ~1.0 GHz, ARMv7-A NEON, 244 MB RAM
+ *   - Display: DRM/KMS only (card0-HDMI-A-1), 1280x720p60. /dev/fb0 is a
+ *     legacy emulation that does NOT drive HDMI (payload-305 black screen
+ *     root cause). Rendering via hwdisp.c DRM dumb buffer + SETCRTC
+ *     (verified 48 FPS on payload-307).
+ *   - Audio: ALSA "rockchip,hdmi" card, i2s-hifi PCM (default).
+ *   - Input: "Twin USB Gamepad" (VID:0810 PID:0001) reports BTN_TRIGGER..
+ *     BTN_BASE4 (0x120..0x129 = codes 288-297), dpad on ABS_HAT0X/Y +
+ *     ABS_X/ABS_Y; "key" gpio-keys device (EV_KEY only).
+ */
